@grand_coalition_stall

Due to our low relations with the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>, coalition talks have stalled and a formal agreement seems increasingly unlikely. Though all is not lost, all democratic parties are expected to lose if another election is called, and the center Marxists have signaled that a toleration agreement might be possible. For better or for worse, the Chancellor for such an arrangement would need to be Heinrich Brüning.

Finally, we could lend an <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>-led cabinet our toleration, it would be incredibly unpopular with both our industrial backers and our voter base, but it may be the only way to save the Republic.

- @spd_toleration_grand: The <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> will tolerate Brüning.
- @dvp_toleration_grand: We will offer the social democrats our toleration.
- @grand_coalition_fail: No compromise can be found.

@spd_toleration_grand
choose-if: spd_relation >= 30 and neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: [? if spd_relation < 30: Our relations are not high enough. ?][? if neo_weimar_coalition < 50: Parties supporting Brüning do not have a majority. ?]
on-arrival: leverage += 5; z_in_government = 1; ddp_in_government = 1 if ddp_exist; dvp_in_government = 1; spd_toleration = 1; spd_patience = (50+0.2*spd_relation) ; in_grand_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; foreign_minister = "Brüning"; foreign_minister_party = "Z"; interior_minister = "Wirth"; interior_minister_party = "Z" if csrp_exist == 0; interior_minister_party = "CSRP" if csrp_exist; interior_minister = "Bolz" if social_catholics_dvp; interior_minister_party = "Z" if social_catholics_dvp; justice_minister = "Guérard"; justice_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser" if ddp_exist; justice_minister_party = ddp_name if ddp_exist; labor_minister = "Stegerwald"; labor_minister_party = "Z"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister = "Hermes"; economic_minister_party = "Z"; finance_minister = "Köhler"; finance_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister = "Hermes"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z";
go-to: ministries

Heinrich Brüning welcomes us into his new cabinet. Now, we have our pick of ministries.

@dvp_toleration_grand
choose-if: neo_weimar_coalition >= 50
unavailable-subtitle: Parties supporting Brüning do not have a majority.
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; z_in_government = 1; ddp_in_government = 1 if ddp_exist; dvp_toleration = 1; in_grand_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; foreign_minister = "Brüning"; foreign_minister_party = "Z"; interior_minister = "Severing"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Guérard"; justice_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser" if ddp_exist; justice_minister_party = ddp_name if ddp_exist; labor_minister = "Wissel"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Köhler"; finance_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister = "Hermes"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich" if ddp_exist; agriculture_minister_party = ddp_name if ddp_exist; industrialist_dissent += 10;

We've agreed to tolerate a Weimar Coalition minority government. Though controversial among even some of our left-leaning members, it may be only way to preserve the republic.

@grand_coalition_fail
on-arrival: grand_coalition_failed = 1

Unfortunately, the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> is unwilling to enter into another coalition with the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> and <span style="color: #69A2BE;">**BVP**</span>, so the grand coalition is unable to be formed.

- @coalition_menu: What are the other governing arrangements?


@left_front
title: A Left Front forms
view-if: left_front >= 50
subtitle: <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span> + [? if sapd_formed: <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SAPD**</span> + ?] <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> ([+ left_front +]%)
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; kpd_in_government = 1; in_left_front = 1; chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister = "Breitscheid"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; interior_minister = "Severing"; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister_party = "SPD"; agriculture_minister = "Baade";

Somehow, the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**Marxists**</span> parties have achieved a majority. They're expected to pursue mass nationalizations, socialization of services, judicial reform, land reform, increased welfare spending and demilitarization. The right-wing paramilitaries are already threatening a putsch [? if President == "Hindenburg": and it seems only a matter of time until President Hindenburg brings this cabinet down ?].


@popular_front
title: An exceptional Popular Front forms
view-if: popular_front >= 50 and kpd_leader = "Luxemburgists" and (z_leader = "Joos" or z_leader = "Kaiser") and left_front < 50
subtitle: <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span> + [? if sapd_formed: <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SAPD**</span> + ?] <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> + [if ddp_exist: <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> +] <span style="color: #000000;">**Z**</span> ([+ popular_front +]%)
on-arrival: spd_in_government = 1; z_in_government = 1; ddp_in_government = 1 if ddp_exist; kpd_in_government = 1; in_popular_front = 1; chancellor = "Breitscheid"; chancellor_party = "SPD"; foreign_minister = "Brüning"; foreign_minister_party = "Z"; interior_minister = "Severing"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Radbruch"; justice_minister_party = "SPD"; labor_minister = "Wissell"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Leber"; reichswehr_minister_party = "SPD"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Hilferding"; agriculture_minister = "Hermes"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; in_popular_front = 1;

The inclusion of the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span> into the governing coalition is unprecedented, but these are exceptional times. Only through the conciliatory leadership of the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span> and the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center**</span> was this governing arrangement able to form. This government is expected to carry out mass nationalizations to solve the crisis, as well as radically reforming Germany's reactionary bureaucracy. The right-wing parties and their paramilitaries have reacted with alarm, and the Conciliatos of the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span> make extensive efforts to assure Germny of their commitment to the Constitutional order.


