@new_grand_coalition
title: A "New Grand Coalition" of all the constitutional parties?
subtitle: <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #000000;">**Z**</span> + <span style="color: #69A2BE;">**BVP**</span> + [? if kvp_formed: <span style="color: #455B95;">**KVP**</span> + ?][? if ddp_exist: <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> + ?] <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> + [? if aspd_exist and aspd_ideology = "Moderate": <span style="color: #FE9E00;">**ASPD**</span> +  ?][? if csrp_exist: <span style="color: #FF6B21;">**CSRP**</span> + ?]<span style="color: #909090;">**Others**</span> ([+ neo_weimar_coalition +]%)
view-if: neo_weimar_coalition >= 50 and grand_coalition < 50
choose-if: z_relation >= 30 and spd_relation >= 30
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #000000;">**Z**</span> + <span style="color: #69A2BE;">**BVP**</span> + [? if kvp_formed: <span style="color: #455B95;">**KVP**</span> + ?][? if ddp_exist: <span style="color: #DCCA4A;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> + ?] <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> + [? if aspd_exist and aspd_ideology = "Moderate": <span style="color: #FE9E00;">**ASPD**</span> +  ?][? if csrp_exist: <span style="color: #FF6B21;">**CSRP**</span> +  ?]<span style="color: #909090;">**Others**</span> ([+ neo_weimar_coalition +]%) - [? if z_relation < 30 : We do not have adequate relations with the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span>. ?][? if spd_relation < 30 : We do not have adequate relations with the <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span>. ?]

In these extraordinary times, with other governing arrangements lacking a majority or the political will, a "New Grand Coalition" might be the only way forward, encompassing all parties right of the <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span> and left of the <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span>, though simply bringing all of these parties together will require effort.

- @use_resources: Use our resources to smooth over the creation of a coalition.
- @coalition_menu: What are the other governing arrangements?

@use_resources
subtitle: -2 resources
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources (need 2).
choose-if: resources >= 2
on-arrival: resources -= 2; leverage -= 5; spd_in_government = 1; z_in_government = 1; ddp_in_government = 1 if ddp_exist; dvp_toleration = 1; in_grand_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Brüning"; chancellor_party = "Z"; foreign_minister = "Brüning"; foreign_minister_party = "Z"; interior_minister = "Severing"; interior_minister_party = "SPD"; justice_minister = "Guérard"; justice_minister_party = "Z"; justice_minister = "Koch-Weser" if ddp_exist; justice_minister_party = ddp_name if ddp_exist; labor_minister = "Wissel"; labor_minister_party = "SPD"; reichswehr_minister = "Groener"; reichswehr_minister_party = "I"; economic_minister = "Schmidt"; economic_minister_party = "SPD"; finance_minister = "Köhler"; finance_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister = "Hermes"; agriculture_minister_party = "Z"; agriculture_minister = "Dietrich" if ddp_exist; agriculture_minister_party = ddp_name if ddp_exist; nationalist_dissent += 10;
go-to: ministries

We transfer some of our campaign funds to our putative coalition partners. Some would call this corruption, but perhaps it is necessary to save our democracy.

Now, we have a new grand coalition, a "Constitutional Coalition" of all the non-fascist and non-communist parties. Nationalists in our party are somewhat skeptical of this arrangement. For better or for worse, Heinrich Brüning is the only viable choice for chancellor.


@far_right_coalition
title: Far-Right Coalition
subtitle: [? if dnvp_ideology ==  "Radical": <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span> + ?][? if dnf_formed: <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> + ?] <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span> ([+ far_right_coalition +]%)
view-if: far_right_coalition >= 50
go-to: far_right_win if (year >= 1932 or nsdap_r >= 44) and president == "Hindenburg"; far_right_fail if (year < 1932 and nsdap_r < 44) and president == "Hindenburg"; far_right_other if president != "Hindenburg"
priority: 2

There are enough votes for the <span style="color: #954B00;">**Nazis**</span> and the [? if dnvp_ideology ==  "Radical": <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span> ?][? if dnf_formed: <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> ?] to form a coalition. [+ nsdap_leader +] has made his participation in government contingent on being appointed chancellor. It is up to President [+ president +] to decide.

@hitler_right_coalition
title: A Right-Wing Coalition including the NSDAP
subtitle: <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> + [? if dnvp_ideology ==  "Radical": <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span> + ?][? if dnf_formed: <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> + ?] <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span> ([+ far_right_coalition +]%) ([+ hitler_right_coalition +]%)
view-if: hitler_right_coalition >= 50 and dvp_ideology == "Right"
go-to: far_right_win if (year >= 1932 or nsdap_r >= 44) and president == "Hindenburg"; far_right_fail if (year < 1932 and nsdap_r < 44) and president == "Hindenburg"; far_right_other if president != "Hindenburg"
priority: 2

With our help, there are enough votes for the <span style="color: #954B00;">**Nazis**</span>, the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span> and the [? if dnvp_ideology ==  "Radical": <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span> ?][? if dnf_formed: <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> ?] to form a coalition. [+ nsdap_leader +] has made his participation in government contingent on being appointed chancellor. It is up to President [+ president +] to decide.

@far_right_win
on-arrival: chancellor = "Hitler"; chancellor_party = "NSDAP"; foreign_minister = 'Neurath'; foreign_minister_party = 'I'; interior_minister = 'Frick'; interior_minister_party = 'NSDAP'; justice_minister = 'Gürtner'; justice_minister_party = 'DNVP' if dnvp_ideology = "Radical"; justice_minister_party = 'DNF' if dnf_formed; labor_minister = 'Seldte'; labor_minister_party = 'DNVP' if dnvp_ideology = "Radical"; labor_minister_party = 'DNF' if dnf_formed; reichswehr_minister = 'Blomberg'; reichswehr_minister_party = 'I'; economic_minister = 'Hugenberg'; economic_minister_party = 'DNVP' if dnvp_ideology = "Radical"; economic_minister_party = 'DNF' if dnf_formed; finance_minister = 'Krosigk'; finance_minister_party = 'I'; agriculture_minister = 'Hugenberg'; agriculture_minister_party = 'DNVP' if dnvp_ideology = "Radical"; agriculture_minister_party = 'DNF' if dnf_formed;

[? if president == "Hindenburg" : President Hindenburg's camarilla ?][? if president != "Hindenburg" : President [+ president +] somehow ?] has decided that the leader of NSDAP must be chancellor [? if president == "Hindenburg": , and the aging president accepts their recommendations. ?][? if president != "Hindenburg" : because it is what the constitution would stipulate. ?]

@far_right_fail
on-arrival: chancellor = "Schleicher"; chancellor_party = "I"; pro_republic -= 10; next_election_time = time + 5; next_election_month = month + 5; next_election_year = year; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12;

The reactionary establishment is still very skeptical of the <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span>, so instead, President Hindenburg appoints Kurt von Schleicher, a former general, as chancellor, to try to "tame" the <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span>.

Schleicher's government is deeply unpopular among all parties of the Reichstag. Despite his support for a coalition with the <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span>, the Nazis want power all to themselves, without Schleicher.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@far_right_other
on-arrival: coup_progress += 2

President [+ president +] faces a dilemma. Is it "democratic" to let democracy be destroyed, if the majority of voters have willed it so? Some, even on the left, suggest that the Nazis would not *truly* be as horrific as their platform suggests, and that giving them power would let them discredit themselves in the eyes of the public.

Alternatively, [+ president +] could use the emergency powers of the presidency. Article 48 has been used by Hindenburg to promulgate anti-democratic and anti-worker policies; can Article 48 be used for good as well as evil?

- @emergency_luther: We will form an emergency government with [+ president +]'s support.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.
- @far_right_win: Let the Nazis form their government.


@no_majority
title: There is no clear governing majority.
view-if: weimar_coalition < 50 and bourgeois_coalition < 50 and (grand_coalition < 50 or grand_coalition_failed == 1) and far_right_coalition < 50
on-arrival: no_majority_elections += 1
go-to: no_majority_bruning if (chancellor != "Papen" and chancellor != "Schleicher" and chancellor != "Hitler"); no_majority_papen if (chancellor = "Papen" and no_majority_papen_elections == 0); no_majority_papen_2 if (chancellor == "Papen" and no_majority_papen_elections > 0); no_majority_schleicher if chancellor == "Schleicher"; no_majority_hitler if chancellor == "Hitler"

# either new elections, or Hindenburg appoints either Brüning, Papen, Schleicher, or Hitler.

@no_majority_bruning
go-to: no_majority_bruning_toleration if (no_majority_elections <= 3 and anti_democratic_coalition <= 50); hindenburg_appoints_papen if no_majority_elections > 3 or anti_democratic_coalition > 50

@no_majority_bruning_toleration
on-arrival: no_majority_bruning_elections += 1

There is no path to a majority government. One option would be to have a continuation of the current Brüning government; if <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> tolerate it, then it would retain a majority vote against no-confidence.

The second option is to have new elections.

- @spd_toleration_grand: The <span style="color: #E3000F;">**SPD**</span> will tolerate Brüning.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.

@hindenburg_appoints_papen
go-to: papen_chancellor

@no_majority_papen
on-arrival: {!
Q.pro_republic -= 5;
Q.no_majority_papen_elections += 1;

Q.next_reichstag_time = Q.rubicon_time + 4;
Q.next_reichstag_week = Q.week + 4;
Q.next_reichstag_month = Q.month;
Q.next_reichstag_year = Q.year;

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_week > 4) {
  Q.next_reichstag_week -= 4;
  Q.next_reichstag_month += 1;
}

if (Q.next_reichstag_month > 12) {
  Q.next_reichstag_month -= 12;
  Q.next_reichstag_year += 1;
}
!}
face-image: img/portraits/PapenFranz.jpg

With the <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span> commanding a strong position in parliament, it can decide the fate of the independent Papen cabinet, as only the [? if dnvp_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span>?][? if dnvp_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>?][? if dvp_papen: and <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span>?] are the only other parties willing to tie themselves to the unpopular chancellor.

However, it's likely that even a coalition of all parties to the right won't receive a majority, not without the support of the antagonistic <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span>. The new Reichstag will convene on [+ next_reichstag_month : month +] [+ next_reichstag_year +], Week [+ next_reichstag_week +].

@no_majority_papen_2
on-arrival: {!
Q.pro_republic -= 5;
Q.no_majority_papen_elections += 1;

Q.next_reichstag_time = Q.rubicon_time + 4;
Q.next_reichstag_week = Q.week + 4;
Q.next_reichstag_month = Q.month;
