face-image: img/portraits/PapenFranz.jpg

There is, once again, no clear path to a majority government. Nevertheless, Hindenburg has reaffirmed his confidence in the chancellor and granted him permission to continue ruling by decree. With the <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span>'s poor electoral performance, the Camarilla is now convinced the party will be more reasonable in its demands and potentially open to tolerating the Papen cabinet.

Negotiations with [+ nsdap_leader +] will resume in the coming weeks. However, Schleicher has begun to lose faith in Papen’s ability to reach an understanding with the <span style="color: #954B00;">Nazis</span>—and if these talks fail, it may be the final straw that turns the schemer against yet another of his old friends.

@no_majority_schleicher
go-to: hitler_chancellor

@no_majority_hitler
on-arrival: in_far_right_coalition = 1; chancellor = "Hitler"; chancellor_party = "NSDAP"; foreign_minister = 'Neurath'; interior_minister = 'Frick'; justice_minister = 'Gürtner'; labor_minister = 'Seldte'; reichswehr_minister = 'Blomberg'; economic_minister = 'Hugenberg'; finance_minister = 'Krosigk'; agriculture_minister = 'Hugenberg'; foreign_minister_party = 'I'; interior_minister_party = 'NSDAP'; justice_minister_party = 'DNVP' if dnvp_ideology = "Radical"; justice_minister_party = 'DNF' if dnf_formed; labor_minister_party = 'DNVP' if dnvp_ideology = "Radical"; labor_minister_party = 'DNF' if dnf_formed; reichswehr_minister_party = 'I'; economic_minister_party = 'DNVP' if dnvp_ideology = "Radical"; economic_minister_party = 'DNF' if dnf_formed; finance_minister_party = 'I'; agriculture_minister_party = 'DNVP' if dnvp_ideology = "Radical"; agriculture_minister_party = 'DNF' if dnf_formed;

President has decided to give Hitler one more chance.


@luthers_dilemma
title: There is no clear governing majority.
subtitle: President [+ president +] faces a dilemma.
view-if: (president_party == dvp_name or president == "Eckener") and (grand_coalition < 50 or grand_coalition_failed == 1)

President [+ president +] faces a dilemma. He desperately desires a democratic government, but the electoral results are not there for such. Article 48 has been used by Hindenburg to promulgate anti-democratic and anti-republican policies; can Article 48 be used for good as well as evil?

- @emergency_luther: We will form an emergency government with [+ president +]'s support.
- @new_elections: We will have new elections.

@emergency_luther
title: We will form an emergency government with [+ president +]'s support.
subtitle: This may have the effect of inflamming public sentiment against us, and the extremists will be against us each step of the way.
on-arrival: sa_strength += 100; sh_strength += 100; rfb_strength += 100; dvp_in_government = 1; chancellor = "Curtius"; chancellor_party = dvp_name; in_emergency_government = 1; foreign_minister_party = dvp_name; foreign_minister = "Stresemann" if no_stresemann == 0; foreign_minister = "Curtius" if no_stresemann; interior_minister_party = dvp_name; interior_minister = "Jarres"; justice_minister_party = dvp_name; justice_minister = "Heinze" if ddp_exist; justice_minister = "Schiffer" if ddp_exist == 0; labor_minister_party = dvp_name; labor_minister = "Thiel"; reichswehr_minister_party = dvp_name; reichswehr_minister = "Seeckt"; economic_minister_party = dvp_name; economic_minister = "Krohne" if ddp_exist; economic_minister = "Hamm" if ddp_exist == 0; finance_minister_party = dvp_name; finance_minister = "Moldenhauer"; agriculture_minister_party = dvp_name; agriculture_minister = "Kanitz";

Yes, an emergency minority government, with the support of the <span style="color: var(--dvp-color);">**[+ dvp_name +]**</span>, led by Julius Curtius

- @far_right_coup
- @emergency_no_confidence: The Nazis immediately call a no-confidence vote against us...

@far_right_coup
title: The far-right parties immediately launch a military coup against us...
view-if: far_right_coalition >= 45
on-arrival: sh_strength += 150; sa_strength += 150; sh_militancy += 0.05; sa_militancy += 0.05

The far-right parties, seeing that we are willing to deny them government by questionably democratic means, have decided that they can only take power by undemocratic means, and have risen up in force against the sitting government.

Their numbers are bolstered by the many government workers who are against the prospect of a unified Socialist government. Police and soldiers defect to the SA and Stahlhelm.

- @civil_war: It is war.

@emergency_no_confidence
title: The Nazis immediately call a no-confidence vote against us...
view-if: far_right_coalition < 45
on-arrival: sa_strength += 200; sh_strength += 200; no_confidence_votes = nsdap_r + kpd_r; no_confidence_votes = no_confidence_votes + spd_r + sapd_r if spd_relation < 45; no_confidence_votes += z_r if z_relation < 45; no_confidence_votes += ddp_r if ddp_relation < 45 and ddp_exist; no_confidence_votes += other_r if (z_relation + dnvp_relation)/2 < 45; no_confidence_succeeds = 1 if no_confidence_votes > 50

The <span style="color: #8B0000;">**KPD**</span>, [? if dnvp_ideology ==  "Radical": <span style="color: #3F7BC1;">**DNVP**</span> + ?][? if dnf_formed: <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> ?] and <span style="color: #954B00;">**NSDAP**</span> will vote against us, of course. The other parties vote their conscience.

In total, [+ no_confidence_votes +]% of the Reichstag is against us. [? if no_confidence_succeeds : We have lost the vote of no confidence. ?]

- @no_confidence_new_elections: There will be new elections, which we will try to delay.
- @no_confidence_win: We have won, for now.

@no_confidence_new_elections
on-arrival: {!
Q.next_election_month = Q.month + 3;
Q.next_election_time = Q.time + 3;
if (Q.next_election_month > 12) {
    Q.next_election_month -= 12;
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year + 1;
} else {
    Q.next_election_year = Q.year;
}
if (Q.chancellor == "Brüning") {
    Q.z_relation -= 5;
}
Q.pro_republic -= 6;
Q.workers_spd -= 5;
Q.new_middle_dvp -= 8;
Q.old_middle_dvp -= 8;
Q.new_middle_ddp -= 5;
Q.old_middle_ddp -= 10;
Q.rural_dbp -= 3;
Q.workers_csvd -= 2;
Q.new_middle_csvd -= 2;
Q.new_middle_kvp -= 3;
Q.old_middle_kvp -= 3;
Q.rural_dnvp -= 5;
Q.workers_nsdap += 5;
Q.old_middle_nsdap += 6;
Q.new_middle_nsdap += 6;
Q.rural_nsdap += 6;
Q.unemployed_nsdap += 5;
// Thresholds are kind of arbitrary - adjusted because of negative economic effects on pro_republic
if (Q.pro_republic < 45 && Q.pro_republic >= 36) {
    Q.workers_spd -= 6;
    Q.new_middle_ddp -= 2;
}
if (Q.pro_republic < 36) {
    // TODO: if you pursue a consistently revolutionary course, you might avoid this? But you might also cause a coalition between Hitler and the Center.
    Q.z_relation -= 5;
    Q.spd_relation -= 5;
    Q.old_middle_dvp *= 0.85;
    Q.workers_dvp -= 2;
    Q.new_middle_dvp -= 5;
    Q.rural_dvp -= 5;
    Q.workers_nsdap += 8;
    Q.old_middle_nsdap += 8;
    Q.new_middle_nsdap += 8;
    Q.rural_nsdap += 8;
    Q.unemployed_nsdap += 8;   
}
if (Q.far_right_coalition >= 50) {
    Q.sa_strength += 100;
    Q.sh_strength += 100;
    Q.coup_progress += 3;
}
!}
go-to: ministries if dvp_in_government
view-if: no_confidence_votes > 50

The next elections are set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@no_confidence_win
